  "note": [
    "Floors for the CI runner. The bench gate reads this file when process.env.CI is true.",
    "",
    "Why the floors are per environment. The harness was first written on the assumption that",
    "measuring this library and the hand-written reference in one process cancels the runner's",
    "speed out of the ratio. The first CI run disproved it: on the array shape this library got",
    "several times slower on the runner while the reference barely moved, and the ratio fell by",
    "two thirds. This library walks while allocating issue objects and an index stack; the",
    "reference is an allocation-free tight loop. Change core count, memory bandwidth or GC and",
    "the two do not slow down together. A ratio cancels out clock speed and nothing else.",
    "",
    "These floors were taken from a single run, so their variance is unknown, and they are set",
    "wide because of it. Record several CI runs, learn the variance, then tighten them.",
    "",
    "singleField is excluded from the ratio gate. The reference's own work there is a couple of",
    "nanoseconds per call, the same order as the harness's own loop overhead, so the ratio stops",
    "meaning 'this library against a hand-written validator' and starts meaning 'this library",
    "against the harness's loop'. The canary that watches for exactly this leaves far less",
    "headroom on singleField than on any other shape, and has fired in CI. It is a measurement",
    "floor, not a threshold to tune. The absolute figures stay in throughput[]."
  ],
